# 1352. Product of the Last K Numbers

**Problem Link:** [Product of the Last K Numbers](https://leetcode.com/problems/product-of-the-last-k-numbers/)

## Approach: Prefix Array

- Maintain a vector `prefix` to store the added numbers.
- Whenever `add(num)` is called, insert the number into the vector.
- For `getProduct(k)`, calculate the starting index as `n - k`.
- Traverse the last `k` elements and multiply them.
- If the product becomes `0`, return `0` immediately.

## Code

```cpp
class ProductOfNumbers {
public:
    vector<int> prefix;

    ProductOfNumbers() {
        prefix.clear();
    }

    void add(int num) {
        prefix.push_back(num);
    }

    int getProduct(int k) {
        int n = prefix.size();
        int pivot = n - k;
        int p = 1;

        for(int i = pivot; i < n; i++) {
            p *= prefix[i];
            if(p == 0) return 0;
        }

        return p;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **add(num):** O(1)
- **getProduct(k):** O(k)
- **Space Complexity:** O(n), where n is the total number of added elements.

## Key Observation

The solution directly multiplies the last `k` elements whenever a query is made. A more optimized approach can use prefix products to achieve O(1) query time.
